{"chunk_id": "24491f3faece", "text": "In a lotus-filled forest retreat, King Pandu\u2014living in exile under a fatal curse that would kill him if he approached his wives in desire\u2014loses control upon seeing Madri and embraces her despite her resistance. The curse immediately takes effect and Pandu dies during the act. Madri mourns over his body until Kunti arrives with the children. The two wives briefly argue over who should perform the ultimate act of devotion by dying with him, but Madri insists, believing she bears responsibility for the fatal moment and trusting Kunti to raise all the children. She ascends the funeral pyre with Pandu. Afterwards, the sages decide that Pandu\u2019s sons must be returned to the Kuru capital. They escort Kunti, the children, and the bodies to Hastinapura, where the royal family and citizens gather to receive them, marking the princes\u2019 return to the political center of the Kuru dynasty.\nPandu, overcome by desire despite a deadly curse, dies with Madri; Madri self-immolates, and sages escort Kunti and the children back to Hastinapura.\nThemes: fatal curse, desire and restraint, widow self-immolation, royal succession, fate and time", "vector": [0.01222060713917017, -0.017659524455666542, -0.0017428946448490024, -0.007527677342295647, -0.02212187647819519, 0.02400718629360199, -0.011142319068312645, -0.007086867466568947, -0.007107212208211422, -0.02315269410610199, 0.016452383249998093, 0.02444121427834034, 0.01989748142659664, 0.034776512533426285, -0.008110902272164822, 0.003743493463844061, 0.04543733224272728, -0.015394438989460468, 0.04275178164243698, -0.015787776559591293, -0.017022045329213142, -0.0011766233947128057, 0.006361226551234722, 0.005418571177870035, -0.030409103259444237, 0.030354849994182587, 0.008938268758356571, -0.02129450999200344, 0.017740903422236443, -0.007480205502361059, -0.01007081102579832, -0.0014122872380539775, 0.006266282871365547, -0.02414282038807869, -0.027886314317584038, 0.00467936